qcap: zero the AM_MEDIA_TYPE fields the wow64 marshaler cannot transfer

On a pure wow64 build the 64-bit unix qcap.so hands an AM_MEDIA_TYPE back
to the 32-bit guest through put_media_type(), which only copies the six
small fields. cbFormat/pbFormat cannot be copied because pbFormat points
into 64-bit memory, so the win32 caller (AMStreamConfig_GetStreamCaps/
GetFormat, VfwPin source_get_media_type) fills them in afterwards. pUnk,
however, is left untouched, so it keeps whatever the uninitialised
CoTaskMemAlloc()'d memory held (often 0xffffffff). FreeMediaType() then
dereferences that bogus pointer and Release()s it, faulting in the app.

ZaloCall hits this as soon as the camera is opened:
  Unhandled exception: page fault on read access to 0xffffffff
  =>0 0x0109176e in zalocall (movl (%ecx), %eax with ecx = 0xffffffff)

Clear pUnk as well as cbFormat/pbFormat so the guest always sees a valid,
empty media type.

--- a/dlls/qcap/v4l.c
+++ b/dlls/qcap/v4l.c
@@ -699,6 +699,12 @@
     mt32->bTemporalCompression = mt->bTemporalCompression;
     mt32->lSampleSize          = mt->lSampleSize;
     mt32->formattype           = mt->formattype;
+    /* pbFormat points into 64-bit memory and is set up by the win32 caller,
+     * but pUnk is never initialised anywhere and would keep stale garbage,
+     * crashing FreeMediaType() on IUnknown_Release(). */
+    mt32->pUnk                 = 0;
+    mt32->cbFormat             = 0;
+    mt32->pbFormat             = 0;
 }
 
 static NTSTATUS wow64_v4l_device_create( void *args )
